{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/903168-border-marches-then-and-now","id":903168,"title":"Border Marches Then and Now","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-29T18:32:52-07:00","id":903168,"title":"Border Marches Then and Now","content":"So Dark Eras gives a long awaited description of the Border Marches. The book indicates that there is no Border Marches in and near civilization. Towns and villages burn it away. What then remains? Is there a barrier like the gauntlet instead or is it more like an absence of space. The way to the Spirit Realm inaccessible from that location because it simply doesn't exist? <br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, if the Border Marches were to return, including paths from a city or town, what would it look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/769-chris-wilson","name":"Chris Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T19:10:31-07:00","id":903188,"title":"","content":"Much like the Astral is, the Border Marches was a realm of layers, labyrinthine, even. Within civilization there's no such spiritual depth. <br /> <br /> In the modern world, with the advance of humanity over nature? Constrained. But cities would probably be walled off city-estates to withstand the depredations of the denizens of the shadow, who would enter our reality far more easily than before, and be an everyday concern to people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https:/